# CelebBoard — Multi-Tenant Celebration Dashboard SaaS

## Project Overview
CelebBoard is a multi-tenant SaaS platform where businesses connect their CRM, Slack, GA4, 
and other systems to display real-time celebrations and KPIs on office TV dashboards.

## Tech Stack
- Next.js 15 (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
- Supabase (Postgres + Realtime + Auth + Storage)
- Zustand for client state, TanStack Query for server state
- Deployed on Vercel (frontend) + Supabase Cloud (backend)

## Architecture Principles
- Multi-tenant: every table has org_id, all queries must be org-scoped
- NEVER write a query without filtering by org_id
- Display pages (/display/[token]) are public, token-authenticated, TV-optimized
- Admin pages (/app/*) require Supabase auth + org membership
- Webhook endpoints (/api/webhooks/[orgId]/[type]) are the ingestion layer
- Integration connectors follow a standard interface pattern (see lib/connectors/)

## Key Patterns
- Celebrations flow: Webhook → Trigger evaluation → Template rendering → Realtime → Display
- KPI data is fetched via connector-specific queries, cached in kpi_definitions.cached_value
- Team members are matched via external_ids jsonb field (hubspot_owner_id, slack_user_id, etc.)
- Display token is a long random string that maps to an org (no login needed on TVs)

## Marketing Site (i18n)
- Marketing pages live in `src/app/[locale]/(marketing)/` (and root `/` at `src/app/page.tsx` for default locale)
- Always use `import { Link } from "@/i18n/navigation"` — NEVER `next/link` in marketing
- Translations in `src/messages/{en,fr}.json` — add keys to BOTH files
- Use `useTranslations("namespace")` in components
- Use `getTranslations()` for `generateMetadata()` in page files
- Middleware only touches marketing routes — `/app`, `/display`, `/api` are excluded

## File Organization
- src/app/page.tsx, src/app/[locale]/(marketing)/ — Public marketing pages (i18n)
- src/app/(auth)/ — Login/signup
- src/app/app/ — Admin pages (authed)
- src/app/display/[token]/ — TV dashboard (public, token-auth)
- src/app/api/webhooks/ — Webhook ingestion
- src/lib/connectors/ — Integration connectors (hubspot, slack, ga4, generic)
- src/lib/db/ — Supabase client, typed queries
- src/lib/celebrations/ — Template rendering, queue logic
- src/components/admin/ — Admin UI components
- src/components/display/ — Dashboard display components

## Coding Conventions
- Use server components by default, 'use client' only when needed
- Use Zod for all API input validation
- Use TypeScript strict mode, no 'any' types
- Prefer named exports over default exports
- Use Supabase RLS for data isolation, don't rely solely on application-level filtering
- Error handling: always handle errors explicitly, show user-friendly messages
